---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How The Tool Shed collects, uses, shares, retains, and protects information across the website and SaaS tools."
  path="/privacy-policy"
>
  <p class="notice">This policy covers thetoolshed.work, Tool Shed accounts, and hosted tools including Video Studio. It does not cover third-party websites you visit through external links.</p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples</th><th>Why we collect it</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Account and contact data</td><td>Email address, display name, authentication provider, account identifiers, and policy acceptance versions and timestamps</td><td>Create and secure your account, document the terms that apply, communicate with you, and provide support</td></tr>
      <tr><td>User content</td><td>Creative briefs, product URLs, project settings, brand details, prompts, generated assets, and quality results</td><td>Provide, save, troubleshoot, and improve the requested service</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Subscription and transaction data</td><td>Plan, subscription status, credits, invoice and payment status, Stripe customer references</td><td>Process purchases, maintain entitlements, prevent fraud, and keep financial records</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Usage and device data</td><td>IP address, browser and device information, request times, pages viewed, feature activity, error and security logs</td><td>Operate, secure, diagnose, and improve the services</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Support communications</td><td>Messages, attachments, and information you send when requesting help</td><td>Respond to and document your request</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Payment card details are collected and processed by Stripe. The Tool Shed does not receive or store your full card number or card security code.</p>

  <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide accounts, projects, generation workflows, credits, subscriptions, and customer support.</li>
    <li>Authenticate users, prevent abuse and fraud, enforce limits, and investigate security incidents.</li>
    <li>Send service messages such as welcome, billing, payment-failure, cancellation, and project-status emails.</li>
    <li>Measure performance and improve the services when you allow optional analytics.</li>
    <li>Comply with legal obligations, enforce our agreements, and protect users and the public.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Legal bases for processing</h2>
  <p>Where a law requires a legal basis, we process information as needed to perform our contract with you, comply with legal obligations, and pursue legitimate interests such as securing, supporting, and improving the services. We rely on consent for optional analytics and other processing when consent is required. You may withdraw consent for future processing without affecting earlier lawful processing.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies">4. Cookies, local storage, and analytics</h2>
  <p>Necessary cookies are used to keep you signed in, protect account routes, and complete authentication. These cookies are required for the service to work. We also store your analytics preference in your browser.</p>
  <p>Google Analytics is optional and loads only after you choose “Allow analytics.” You can change that choice at any time using <button type="button" data-cookie-settings>Cookie Settings</button> in the footer. When a browser sends a recognized Global Privacy Control signal and no preference has been saved, we default to necessary-only storage.</p>

  <h2>5. Service providers and disclosures</h2>
  <p>We disclose information only as needed to operate the services, complete a transaction, comply with law, or protect rights and safety. Providers may include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Netlify</strong> for web hosting, delivery, security controls, and server functions.</li>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> for authentication, databases, and application storage.</li>
    <li><strong>Stripe</strong> for checkout, subscriptions, invoices, fraud controls, and payment processing.</li>
    <li><strong>Brevo and n8n</strong> for transactional email and service automation.</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> for optional sign-in and, with consent, analytics.</li>
    <li><strong>AI and media-processing providers</strong> selected to produce requested outputs when generation features are enabled.</li>
    <li>Professional advisers, authorities, or transaction counterparties when reasonably necessary for legal, accounting, security, or business-transfer purposes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal information. We do not share personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising. We do not use sensitive personal information to infer characteristics about you.</p>

  <h2>6. AI processing and user content</h2>
  <p>When you request an AI feature, relevant inputs and settings may be sent to a selected provider to create or evaluate the output. Do not upload confidential, regulated, or third-party material unless you have authority to use and disclose it. Provider processing and retention may vary by service and configuration.</p>

  <h2>7. Retention</h2>
  <p>We keep account and project data while your account is active and as reasonably needed to provide the service. You may delete individual Video Studio projects and, after active subscriptions are resolved, delete your Tool Shed account. We may retain limited transaction, fraud, security, backup, and legal records where required or permitted by law. Backup copies are removed on their normal rotation schedule.</p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>We use access controls, encrypted transport, hosted payment processing, row-level database rules, rate limits, logging, and other reasonable safeguards. No system is perfectly secure. You are responsible for using a strong, unique password and protecting access to your email and account.</p>

  <h2>9. Your choices and privacy rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to know, access, correct, export, delete, or restrict certain uses of personal information, and to appeal a denied request. We will not discriminate against you for exercising an applicable privacy right.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Signed-in users can export Video Studio account data from the <a href="/account">Account</a> page.</li>
    <li>Signed-in users can delete eligible accounts from the Account page.</li>
    <li>Anyone may submit a request through <a href="/privacy-choices">Privacy Choices</a> or email <a href="mailto:hello@thetoolshed.work?subject=Privacy%20request">hello@thetoolshed.work</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may verify your identity before fulfilling a request. Some information may be exempt from deletion or disclosure, including records we must retain for legal, security, tax, fraud-prevention, or dispute purposes. Where applicable, you may also object to or restrict processing, withdraw consent, request data portability, and complain to your local data-protection authority.</p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>The services are intended for adults and are not directed to children under 13. Paid Tool Shed accounts are for people age 18 or older. If you believe a child provided personal information, contact us so we can investigate and delete it where appropriate.</p>

  <h2>11. International use</h2>
  <p>The Tool Shed is operated from the United States. If you use the services elsewhere, information may be processed in the United States and other locations where our providers operate. Where required, we and our providers rely on recognized transfer mechanisms or contractual safeguards for cross-border processing.</p>

  <h2>12. Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy as the services or law changes. Material changes will be identified by a new effective date and, when appropriate, an account or email notice.</p>
  <p>The Tool Shed is the operator responsible for the processing described here. Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:hello@thetoolshed.work?subject=Privacy%20question">hello@thetoolshed.work</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
